::'''Hanya:''' As for how many floors there are...? Well, not even us judges know for sure.
::'''Hanya:''' But there's a legend among us judges that a short-life prisoner once tried to escape but ended up falling into the depths... and when we found him at the bottom, he was already an old man on the brink of death...
::'''Hanya:''' Did he spend his whole life falling? Or did some long-life prisoner drain his life essence? We'll never know. Anyway, please don't try anything like that.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why keep the terrain so dangerous?
::'''Hanya:''' You're funny, (Trailblazer). This prison does contain many layers. We even brought in Vidyadhara Ichor Line craftsmen to introduce the ingenuity of delve enchantment. What you're seeing now is just one part of The Shackling Prison.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Is that true, Dan Heng?
::'''Dan Heng:''' Perhaps. Judging from the appearance, much of the architecture in this prison has a Vidyadharan style... So perhaps they did have a hand in building this place back then.
::'''Hanya:''' Well, the paths here serve as both passageways for the Ten-Lords Commission and barriers for the prisoners.
::'''Hanya:''' Most prisoners locked up here have committed serious crimes violating the Xianzhou Legal Code, and many of them are Denizens of Abundance like borisin, houyhnhnm, and {{Rubi|wingweavers|featherines}}. To be honest, these abominations... are pretty good at trying to break out.
::'''Hanya:''' So, as long as the treacherous terrain here makes it harder for them to escape, the Ten-Lords Commission doesn't have any complaints.
:'''Hanya:''' Please come this way.

